  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "No scalar of the Vite config is readable. base, root, publicDir, cacheDir, envDir, envPrefix, appType, logLevel, build.outDir, build.assetsDir, build.target, build.sourcemap, server.host, server.open, server.origin, resolve.alias, server.proxy and build.rollupOptions.input are keys of an object literal passed to defineConfig, and the JavaScript and TypeScript Packs publish no fact for an object key whose value is a string, an array or a nested object -- only for a key whose value is a function, as definition.method.",
      "A plugin call cannot be tied to the package that supplied it. import.module spans the specifier string and the local binding (import.default in omega-javascript, binding.import_default in omega-typescript) spans the identifier; neither span contains the other, and neither publishes a field naming the other side. uses_plugin therefore names the factory that was called, not the package it came from.",
      "Call arguments are published by no Pack, so loadEnv's prefix and directory, createServer's inline config and a plugin factory's options are unreachable.",
      "import.meta.env is a member expression and emits no fact; import.meta.glob() emits call.method named glob, which is indistinguishable from any other .glob() call, so glob imports are not claimed.",
      "Plugin execution order, transform output, the generated module graph and dev-server middleware behaviour are runtime semantics."
    ]
  },
